01:02:16,363 --> 01:02:22,363
Unbroken is a 2014 American war drama film produced and directed by Angelina Jolie and
written by the Coen brothers, Richard LaGravenese, and William Nicholson.

11
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:36,000
It is based on the non-fiction book by Laura Hillenbrand, Unbroken: A World
War II Story of Survival, Resilience, and Redemption (2010).

12
01:14:43,636 --> 01:14:49,636
The film stars Jack O'Connell as Army officer Louis "Louie" Zamperini, an American
Olympian, and Miyavi as Imperial Japanese Army (IJA) corporal Mutsuhiro Watanabe.

13
01:20:57,272 --> 01:21:03,272
Zamperini survived in a raft for 47 days after his bomber ditched in the ocean during the Second World War,
before being captured by the Japanese and being sent to a series of prisoner of war camps.

14
01:27:10,909 --> 01:27:16,909
Filming took place in Australia from October 2013 to February 2014.

15
01:33:24,545 --> 01:33:30,545
Unbroken had its world premiere in Sydney on November 17, 2014, followed by a
London premiere at the Odeon Leicester Square on November 26, 2014.

16
01:39:38,181 --> 01:39:44,181
The film was released in the United States on December 25, 2014.

17
01:45:51,818 --> 01:45:57,818
It received mixed reviews from critics, though praise was given to
O'Connell's performance and Deakins's cinematography.

18
01:52:05,454 --> 01:52:11,454
It was a financial success, grossing $163 million worldwide.

19
01:58:19,090 --> 01:58:25,090
The film was followed by a less succesfull sequel,
Unbroken: Path to Redemption, in 2018.

